![CDATA[More than 99% of California’s sunflower sea stars vanished, now scientists have found a mysterious colony that could help revive dying kelp forests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133200597.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ten years ago, sunflower sea stars faced near extinction due to a devastating marine epidemic, leading to unchecked sea urchin populations that destroyed essential kelp forests. Recently, a newly identified colony of these sea stars has rekindled hope for ecological restoration. Researchers are examining their resilience to diseases, which could greatly benefit efforts to reintroduce these vital predators to their ocean habitats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/more-than-99-of-californias-sunflower-sea-stars-vanished-now-scientists-have-found-a-mysterious-colony-that-could-help-revive-dying-kelp-forests/articleshow/133200597.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/more-than-99-of-californias-sunflower-sea-stars-vanished-now-scientists-have-found-a-mysterious-colony-that-could-help-revive-dying-kelp-forests/articleshow/133200597.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:02:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133200760,imgsize-137685.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota church closes after 70 years, gives $600,000 to nonprofits and supports housing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133160367.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[St. Mark's United Church of Christ closed after seven decades due to declining membership.  The congregation distributed approximately $600,000 among 21 local nonprofits.  A substantial gift of $115,000 went to Loaves &amp; Fishes for meal provision.  The church property will be redeveloped into affordable housing units for the community.  This act ensures the church's legacy continues through support and new homes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-last-act-of-kindness-a-minnesota-church-closed-after-its-congregation-fell-to-26-members-then-gave-about-600000-to-nonprofits-and-sold-its-property-for-affordable-housing/articleshow/133160367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-last-act-of-kindness-a-minnesota-church-closed-after-its-congregation-fell-to-26-members-then-gave-about-600000-to-nonprofits-and-sold-its-property-for-affordable-housing/articleshow/133160367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:10:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133160671,imgsize-718369.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ireland’s vanished rainforest is getting a second chance with 30,000 trees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133199605.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-ancient-rainforest-vanished-after-thousands-of-years-of-human-activity-now-nearly-30000-trees-are-being-planted-to-bring-it-back/articleshow/133199605.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-ancient-rainforest-vanished-after-thousands-of-years-of-human-activity-now-nearly-30000-trees-are-being-planted-to-bring-it-back/articleshow/133199605.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133200166,imgsize-247985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian family turns remote sheep farm island into $4.8m wildlife haven]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133199043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-family-bought-a-remote-island-to-run-a-sheep-farm-now-they-are-turning-it-into-a-4-8-million-conservation-sanctuary-for-endangered-wildlife/articleshow/133199043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-family-bought-a-remote-island-to-run-a-sheep-farm-now-they-are-turning-it-into-a-4-8-million-conservation-sanctuary-for-endangered-wildlife/articleshow/133199043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T11:31:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133200024,imgsize-1943232.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Putin’s first Kuril Islands visit matters as Russia-Japan ties hit new low]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133198569.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Russian President Vladimir Putin visited the disputed Kuril Islands for the first time.  This visit occurred amid deeply strained relations between Russia and Japan.  Japan strongly protests the visit, reiterating its territorial claims over the islands.  The long-standing dispute has intensified since Russia's invasion of Ukraine.  This territorial disagreement prevents a formal World War II peace treaty.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/why-putins-first-kuril-islands-visit-matters-as-russia-japan-ties-hit-new-low/articleshow/133198569.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https