entagon-review/articleshow/133197963.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/us-attack-on-yemen-killed-153-civilians-in-april-2025-pentagon-review/articleshow/133197963.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T10:13:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133199062,imgsize-115014.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1960, 2-day-old David Stevenson was found abandoned; 66 years later, he finds his family]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133188402.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David Stevenson, who was found abandoned as a two-day-old baby in a London flats corridor in 1960, has finally discovered his biological family more than six decades later. Appearing on This Morning, David opened up about his emotional search, meeting his relatives in the Netherlands and learning more about his biological mother, Petra.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/in-1960-2-day-old-baby-david-stevenson-was-found-abandoned-in-a-london-flats-corridor-66-years-later-he-finally-discovers-his-biological-family/articleshow/133188402.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/in-1960-2-day-old-baby-david-stevenson-was-found-abandoned-in-a-london-flats-corridor-66-years-later-he-finally-discovers-his-biological-family/articleshow/133188402.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T22:13:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133188486,imgsize-62572.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Missile threat made Trump move to smaller US jet during Turkey visit: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133196786.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Trump was secretly moved to a smaller aircraft due to a missile threat. This extraordinary security operation occurred during his return from Turkey last month. The larger presidential plane was used as a decoy while he traveled separately. Secret Service acted on credible and imminent intelligence regarding the danger. The operation remained secret to conceal the president's movements from potential attackers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/missile-threat-made-donald-trump-move-to-smaller-us-jet-during-turkey-visit-report/articleshow/133196786.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/missile-threat-made-donald-trump-move-to-smaller-us-jet-during-turkey-visit-report/articleshow/133196786.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T09:02:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133196827,imgsize-66794.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Virginia rebuilt 1.09 miles of shoreline, creating new marsh and oyster reef in Chesapeake Bay]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133194062.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Virginia’s $8 million Ragged Island restoration project rebuilt 1.09 miles of shoreline, creating 2.6 acres of marsh and 2.2 acres of oyster reef. Funded by NOAA Fisheries, the project is reducing erosion and keeping hundreds of tons of sediment and nutrients out of Chesapeake Bay while creating valuable habitat for fish, crabs and birds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2025-virginia-spent-8-million-rebuilding-1-09-miles-of-ragged-island-shoreline-the-project-created-2-6-acres-of-new-marsh-and-2-2-acres-of-oyster-reef-while-cutting-hundreds-of-tons-of-sediment-entering-chesapeake-bay/articleshow/133194062.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2025-virginia-spent-8-million-rebuilding-1-09-miles-of-ragged-island-shoreline-the-project-created-2-6-acres-of-new-marsh-and-2-2-acres-of-oyster-reef-while-cutting-hundreds-of-tons-of-sediment-entering-chesapeake-bay/articleshow/133194062.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T03:52:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133195057,imgsize-160183.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Louisiana creates 1,170 acres of wetlands; shrimp and crabs return to restored habitat after a year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133192949.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Louisiana’s Upper Barataria Marsh Creation Project has restored 1,170 acres of new wetland habitat in the Barataria Basin. One year after construction, white and brown shrimp, blue crab and red drum are using the restored marsh and water features. The project aims to rebuild coastal ecosystems damaged by decades of land loss and the Deepwater Horizon oil spill.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/louisiana-created-1170-acres-of-new-wetlands-in-barataria-basin-one-year-later-shrimp-and-crabs-are-returning-to-the-restored-habitat/articleshow/133192949.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/louisiana-created-1170-acres-of-new-wetlands-in-barataria-basin-one-year-later-shrimp-and-crabs-are-returning-to-the-restored-habitat/articleshow/133192949.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T02:52:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="htt